# PHP & Git conventions

## New PHP files

Every new PHP file MUST start with:

```php
<?php

declare(strict_types=1);
```

Then optional file docblock with the repository author:

```php
/**
 * @author rooneyi <22ki129@esisalama.org>
 */
```

Then `namespace`, then the type declaration (`final class`, `interface`, `enum`, or `trait`).

Do not omit `declare(strict_types=1);`.

## Git commits

- Author and committer must be: `rooneyi <22ki129@esisalama.org>`
- Never add `Co-authored-by:` trailers (including Cursor)
- Never use the agent identity as author or committer
